{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSbPQZNyLvU5YRxAf2pr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! All tests passed. **Command**: `./mvnw test` from `sample-service/` directory. **Result**: 20 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n<<PHASE:REVIEW>>\n\nLet me review the changes against the acceptance criteria and verify the implementation is correct.\n\n**Acceptance criteria mapping:**\n\n1. **Existing build passes** ✓ - BUILD SUCCESS with no failures\n2. **Existing tests pass** ✓ - All baseline tests from OrderControllerTest and ShipmentControllerTest still pass\n3. **`POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel` cancels an active order, persists it, and cancels that order's `CREATED` shipments** ✓ - Implemented in OrderController.cancel(), test \"cancels an active order and returns 200\" and \"cancels created shipments when cancelling an order\"\n4. **Error responses are consistent with the rest of this API** ✓ - Using ConflictException (409) and ResourceNotFoundException (404) with ErrorCode enum, consistent with existing patterns\n5. **A repeated cancel succeeds; a cancel blocked by a `CONFIRMED` shipment changes nothing; an unknown order is refused; a shipment for a cancelled order is refused** ✓ - Tests: \"cancel is idempotent\", \"cancel returns 409 if any shipment is confirmed\", \"cancel returns 404\", \"rejects creating a shipment for a cancelled order\"\n6. **No new Maven dependency appears** ✓ - No changes to pom.xml, only used existing dependencies\n7. **No unrelated production file changes** ✓ - Only modified Order.kt, OrderController.kt, ShipmentController.kt, and their repositories/API error classes as needed\n\n**Diff review:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Added `status: OrderStatus = OrderStatus.ACTIVE` field and `OrderStatus` enum. ✓ Necessary to track order state.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** - No changes needed (it was ShipmentRepository that needed changes).\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Added `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method. ✓ Necessary to find shipments by order to cancel them.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** - \n   - Added `shipmentRepository: InMemoryShipmentRepository` injection ✓ Necessary for accessing shipments\n   - Added `cancel(@PathVariable orderId: String)` endpoint ✓ Implements the requirement\n   - Logic: check order exists (404), return if already cancelled (idempotent), check for CONFIRMED shipments (409), cancel order and CREATED shipments ✓ All requirements met\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** - \n   - Added `orderRepository: InMemoryOrderRepository` injection ✓ Necessary for checking order status\n   - Added check in create endpoint for cancelled orders ✓ Implements the requirement to reject with 409 for cancelled orders\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** - Added `ORDER_CANCELLED` error code to ErrorCode enum ✓ Necessary for error responses\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - \n   - Added `shipmentRepository: InMemoryShipmentRepository` injection\n   - Updated `reset()` to clear shipmentRepository\n   - Added 5 new tests: cancel active order, cancel with shipment cancellation, idempotent cancel, cancel with confirmed shipment conflict, cancel non-existent order, created order has ACTIVE status\n   - All tests follow existing patterns ✓\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - \n   - Added `orderRepository: InMemoryOrderRepository` injection\n   - Updated `reset()` to clear orderRepository\n   - Added 1 new test: reject creating shipment for cancelled order\n   - Test follows existing patterns ✓\n\n**Unresolved findings:** None. All acceptance criteria are met, error handling is consistent, and the implementation follows the existing patterns in the codebase.\n\n<<PHASE:DONE>>\n\n```\nRequirement   Add POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel endpoint to transition orders from ACTIVE to CANCELLED status, cancel associated CREATED shipments, handle idempotent retries, reject with 409 if any shipment is CONFIRMED, reject with 404 for missing orders, and prevent shipment creation for cancelled orders.\n\nChanged       Order.kt - Added status field and OrderStatus enum (ACTIVE, CANCELLED)\n              ShipmentRepository.kt - Added findByOrderId() method to retrieve shipments for an order\n              OrderController.kt - Added cancel endpoint with full logic (check exists, idempotent, conflict detection, cascade cancel)\n              ShipmentController.kt - Added check to reject shipment creation for cancelled orders\n              ApiError.kt - Added ORDER_CANCELLED error code to ErrorCode enum\n              OrderControllerTest.kt - Added 5 new tests covering all cancel scenarios (success, idempotent, conflict, not found, active status)\n              ShipmentControllerTest.kt - Added 1 test for rejecting shipment creation on cancelled order\n\nTests         1. Cancel ACTIVE order successfully - verifies order transitions to CANCELLED\n              2. Cascade cancel CREATED shipments - verifies CREATED shipments are cancelled when order is cancelled\n              3. Idempotent cancel - verifies repeated cancellation succeeds without error\n              4. Conflict with CONFIRMED shipment - verifies 409 rejection and no state change when shipment is CONFIRMED\n              5. Not found - verifies 404 for non-existent orders\n              6. ACTIVE status on creation - verifies newly created orders have ACTIVE status\n              7. Reject shipment for cancelled order - verifies 409 when creating shipment for cancelled order\n\nVerification  Command: ./mvnw test from sample-service/\n              Result: 20 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS\n              All existing tests continue to pass; new tests verify all cancel scenarios\n\nNot done      Nothing - all acceptance criteria implemented and verified\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3331,"cache_rea